    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0534" n="444" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg444"/>

                <head>No. 207.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Washburne.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 23,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 652.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 651, of the
                    21st instant, I have to inform you that the watch intended to be restored to the
                    family of General Lafayette will be forwarded to you in a separate package by
                    this mail; and you are requested to ascertain the eldest male representative of
                    General Lafayette, and to restore the watch to him as the representative of the
                    family, in accordance with the provisions of the act of Congress.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
